64
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:27,943
So a little more detail on what the source
step does for the poky/oe-unit-build-env.

65
00:04:27,943 --> 00:04:32,736
It uses the source command for
bash which is a synonym for the dot.

66
00:04:32,736 --> 00:04:34,660
So if you've seen dot space and

67
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:39,038
then the name of the script before,
that's exactly the same syntax.

68
00:04:39,038 --> 00:04:42,762
And what this really just means is that
any of the variables that are created or

69
00:04:42,762 --> 00:04:45,857
modified by the script that you
source is going to remain available

70
00:04:45,857 --> 00:04:47,080
after the script edits.

71
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:50,248
So it's going to run in the same
sub shell, in other words,

72
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:53,551
everything defined inside
oe-init-build-env in terms

73
00:04:53,551 --> 00:04:58,055
of environment variables is going to be
